Contribute to this project: Normalize the twenty fixed public seed-0 source records independently. The platform merges identical entity keys, resolves attributes by source priority, preserves ties and missing identities, and returns the global catalog with provenance.

Your assigned work unit is entirely contained in the JSON packet below. No project checkout, materials directory, network lookup or other contribution is needed. You may use reference_work/ as scratch space. Submit only your assigned artifact.

{
  "task_id": "normalize-sku-0000-14",
  "title": "Normalize SKU-0000-14",
  "artifact_kind": "json",
  "optional": false,
  "description": "Normalize exactly one supplier record into an identity and attribute observation.",
  "requirements": "Process only the supplied record. Use the brand_aliases display value. Model: remove only spaces/hyphens and uppercase; retain suffixes such as S. pack_size is an integer or \"N pcs\". Do not infer missing identity fields from title. If model is empty/missing use reason missing_model; otherwise if pack_size is null/empty use missing_pack_size. An unresolved result contains ONLY source_sku, source_row (row_id), source, priority (source_priority[source]), entity_id:null, reason. Otherwise return these fields plus brand, model, category, pack_size, attributes, with reason:null. Convert attribute capacity to capacity_gb (decimal TB=1000 GB), length to length_mm (m=1000 mm, cm=10 mm), power to power_w (mW=0.001 W); all resulting numbers are integers. Normalize connector/interface with attribute_aliases, lowercase color, retain other attributes. entity_id = BRAND_UPPER:MODEL:category:packN; append :gbN for storage or :mmN for cables. Do not resolve conflicts with other records; that is platform assembly work.",
  "material_paths": [],
  "packet": {
    "version": 1,
    "operation": "normalize_one_record",
    "runtime": "json",
    "dependencies": [],
    "input": {
      "record": {
        "row_id": "C0000-14",
        "source_sku": "SKU-0000-14",
        "source": "marketplace",
        "brand": "Halo Electronics",
        "model": "hc-500s",
        "category": "cable",
        "pack_size": "1 pcs",
        "title": "Halo HC500S new edition",
        "attributes": {
          "length": "500 cm",
          "connector": "usb c"
        }
      },
      "rules": {
        "brand_aliases": {
          "LUMEN": "Lumen",
          "ORION": "Orion",
          "HALO": "Halo",
          "ZEPHYR": "Zephyr",
          "Lumen Electronics": "Lumen",
          "Orion Electronics": "Orion",
          "Halo Electronics": "Halo",
          "Zephyr Electronics": "Zephyr"
        },
        "source_priority": {
          "manufacturer": 0,
          "distributor": 1,
          "marketplace": 2
        },
        "model_normalization": "Uppercase and remove only spaces and hyphens; retain all letters and digits including suffix S.",
        "unit_rules": {
          "capacity": "decimal: 1 TB = 1000 GB; GB remains GB",
          "length": "1 m = 1000 mm; 1 cm = 10 mm",
          "power": "1 W = 1000 mW"
        },
        "attribute_aliases": {
          "usb c": "USB-C",
          "USB-C": "USB-C",
          "nvme": "NVMe",
          "NVMe": "NVMe"
        }
      }
    },
    "output": {
      "shape": {
        "source_sku": "string",
        "source_row": "original row_id",
        "source": "string",
        "priority": "integer",
        "entity_id": "canonical string or null",
        "reason": "null|missing_model|missing_pack_size",
        "resolved_only": {
          "brand": "canonical display string",
          "model": "normalized string",
          "category": "string",
          "pack_size": "integer",
          "attributes": "normalized attribute object"
        }
      }
    },
    "examples": []
  }
}

You are authorized to submit the result to the local TaskForge service. Create payload.json with the following envelope (replace the example with the actual result; artifact file paths are relative to the project, without materials/ or reference_work/ prefixes):
{"task_id": "normalize-sku-0000-14", "artifact": {"kind": "json", "value": "your result"}}
Send with: curl --unix-socket /workspace/.collector.sock -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-binary @payload.json http://collector/submit
Inspect the returned receipt; correct invalid results if needed.
